{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"agent_message","text":"The exploration produced the suspected discrepancy: node 2 applied the later write at index 6, then removed node 1 returned a ReadState at index 4 while its application still held the old value. With stepdown enabled, node 1 returned no read state.\n\nI’ll construct a fresh safety check that tests certificates only when one is returned. The control may remain pending; it does not need to succeed.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > make_check9.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));c=[x for x in r['candidates'] if x['id']=='fa267c61288944acbf9df7f94f7681d6'][0];q=c['question'];q['disposition']='ready_for_check';q['unknowns']=['Fresh fixed observations and correspondence must verify write-before-read ordering, returned context and applicable ReadOnlySafe responsibility.'];q['trigger_rationale']='Exploration 2b93f866725c4c13ac2c78db651dcb67 executed the full removal/successor history without fabricated protocol state: old node returned index 4 after new node applied index 6. Enabled stepdown returned no certificate. Fix a safety implication so permitted pending behavior is not mistaken for failure.'\nclaim=dict(id='c_removed_read_fence',kind='obligation',concern='consensus_safety',description='Under ReadOnlySafe, any returned read-index certificate for a new read must provide a safe log-prefix fence for that read: it must not certify a local prefix excluding a write completed before read invocation in the same Raft history. Removal without immediate stepdown may cause refusal or pending behavior, but must not cause an obsolete former leader to issue a stale safety certificate.',source_ids=['s_read_safety','s_read_contract','s_raw_read','s_removal_option'],scope=dict(description='Live, unstopped RawNode using ReadOnlySafe and StepDownOnRemoval=false, after actual removal into a different singleton voter configuration; successor write completes before a unique read request on the old node.',assumptions=['Caller persists and applies Ready work in order before Advance; no storage failures or crashes.','A write completes only when the retained current voter applies its committed write; read invocation follows that completion.','Read request context is unique; the library node remains unstopped and no embedding-layer read rejection is assumed.'],excluded=['Applications that stop or reject all reads after local removal.','ReadOnlyLeaseBased, context reuse, early Advance, fabricated terms or progress.','An obligation to return a result when the request is dropped or pending.','Production embedding endpoints, wall-clock deadlines and arbitrary crash recovery.']),pending=[],grounding=dict(source_ids=['s_leader_admit','s_tracker','s_config_commit','s_load_read','s_removal_option','s_node_read_route','s_node_read_entry'],expectation_ids=['s_read_safety','s_read_contract','s_raw_read'],binding_ids=['bind_singleton_read','bind_removal_read'],derivation='ReadOnlySafe promises linearizable read safety; Node and RawNode ReadIndex describe a returned index as the fence after which prior read requests may safely be processed. In a single log history with a completed write before invocation, a certificate for an earlier prefix cannot suffice when the local application also excludes that write. The API permits lost requests, so the requirement is implication from emitted certificate, not guaranteed success. StepDownOnRemoval is optional and contains no disclaimer weakening ReadOnlySafe when false. The inspected interfaces impose no immediate shutdown or read-rejection duty on removal; Node itself blocks proposals but routes reads independently.',applicability='Actual removal was committed and applied before the surviving voter campaigns and applies a later write. No higher-term message is forged or suppressed: the new singleton has no reason to send to removed nodes. The old node is queried before periodic quorum loss changes its role, a legal ordering of asynchronous inputs.',unresolved=[],conflicts=[],alternatives=['StepDownOnRemoval=true causes pending/no-certificate behavior in this history and is a valid protection.','Embedding applications may stop removed nodes, limiting exposure; that does not establish protection in the selected live-library scope.','A later CheckQuorum may step down, but future role correction cannot justify an earlier unsafe certificate.']))\nbind=[]\nfor i,mat,sym,a,b,desc in [('bind_singleton_read','s_leader_admit','stepLeader',1356,1379,'Singleton ReadIndex bypasses quorum and current-term commit checks.'),('bind_removal_read','s_config_commit','switchToConfig',1983,2007,'Removal only forces follower transition under stepDownOnRemoval.')]:\n bind.append(dict(id=i,material_id=mat,symbol=sym,start_line=a,end_line=b,description=desc,pending=[],associations=[dict(claim_id=claim['id'],source_ids=claim['source_ids'],rationale='This branch establishes or consumes the authority context for a read certificate governed by ReadOnlySafe.')]))\ncs=dict(action='obligation',candidate_id=c['id'],question=q,obligation=claim,bindings=bind,rationale='Fix a certificate-safety implication after same-history exploration; do not require success from the stepdown control.')\ns=Path('removed_read_explore_test.go').read_text().replace('TestAssuranceExploreRemovedRead','TestAssuranceRemovedReadFence')\ns=s.replace('writeIndex:=uint64(0)','writeIndex:=uint64(0)\\\\n   readID:=\\\"read-after-write-\\\"+name')\ns=s.replace('\\\"event\\\":stage,\\\"case\\\":name,','\\\"event\\\":stage,\\\"case\\\":name,\\\"read_id\\\":readID,\\\"read_returned\\\":len(reads[1])>0,\\\"covers_completed_write\\\":false,')\ns=s.replace('x[\\\"read_context\\\"]=string(reads[1][len(reads[1])-1].RequestCtx)','x[\\\"read_context\\\"]=string(reads[1][len(reads[1])-1].RequestCtx);x[\\\"covers_completed_write\\\"]=reads[1][len(reads[1])-1].Index>=writeIndex;x[\\\"applied_through_fence\\\"]=applied[1]>=reads[1][len(reads[1])-1].Index')\ns=s.replace('emit(\\\"write_completed_before_read\\\")\\\\n   nodes[1].ReadIndex([]byte(\\\"unique-read-after-write\\\"));pump();emit(\\\"after_read_drain\\\")','emit(\\\"write_completed\\\")\\\\n   emit(\\\"read_admitted\\\")\\\\n   nodes[1].ReadIndex([]byte(readID));pump();emit(\\\"read_result\\\")')\nPath('removed_read_check_test.go').write_text(s)\ng=dict(source_ids=['s_leader_admit','s_tracker','s_config_commit','s_load_read','s_raw_read'],expectation_ids=['s_read_safety','s_read_contract','s_raw_read'],binding_ids=['bind_singleton_read','bind_removal_read'],derivation='For c_removed_read_fence, a returned certificate must cover the already completed write. covers_completed_write is computed from the actual returned index and actual write-entry index; neither value is chosen from an expected outcome. The result record is unconditional after processing Ready, and read_returned selects the necessary safety antecedent. A missing certificate is permitted and must not fail this implication. Observed old application value and applied-through-fence diagnostic independently expose whether the lower fence permits stale local state.',applicability='Correlated write completion and read invocation in one actual log history. Unique read_id is present at both prerequisites and result; its identity is independent of read index, term or the value compared.',unresolved=[],conflicts=[],alternatives=['No returned certificate under the stepdown control is a bounded absence of unsafe certification, not successful read completion.'])\nplan=dict(description='Fresh fixed three-node election and joint removal of nodes 1 and 3. Apply automatic exit on all nodes, campaign singleton 2, replicate/apply a set-one write, then invoke a unique ReadIndex on removed node 1. Observe every returned ReadState and application state after draining. Repeat with StepDownOnRemoval=true; permit no result.',claim_id=claim['id'],binding_ids=['bind_singleton_read','bind_removal_read'],harness=dict(kind='go_test',source='',files={},description='Actual RawNode instances and emitted messages with no packet loss, no ticks needed between successor write completion and read, no target-state mutation. MemoryStorage models persisted state in a no-crash run; integer application state changes only when actual committed set-one entries are applied.',semantic_changes=['In-package observation reads local role/configuration and ReadStates; no protocol logic changes.','Driver supplies synchronous storage, ordered application and reliable transport.','Identical genesis snapshots configure the original three voters.'],prerequisites=[dict(alias='write',event='write_completed',conditions=[dict(field='new_value',op='eq',value=1),dict(field='new_applied',op='eq',reference='write_index')]),dict(alias='admission',event='read_admitted',conditions=[dict(field='write_index',op='eq',reference='write.write_index')])],legality=dict(source_ids=['s_ready','s_advance','s_bootstrap','s_init','s_apply_contract','s_config_commit','s_node_read_route','s_node_read_entry','s_removal_option'],expectation_ids=['s_read_contract','s_raw_read','s_apply_contract'],binding_ids=['bind_singleton_read','bind_removal_read'],derivation='All methods run sequentially. Ready persistence/application precede Advance and delivery. Membership transitions come solely from committed entries. The single surviving voter uses Campaign and its persistence-delayed self-vote rather than a fabricated election. Its set-one application establishes write completion before read admission. Removal does not stop the live RawNode; optional stepdown, proposal blocking and independent read dispatch are explicit source mechanisms. Timers need not intervene between two finite consecutive API operations, and no network message to the old node is withheld.',applicability='ReadOnlySafe; CheckQuorum=true; StepDownOnRemoval toggled as the only control difference. No stale read contexts, failed storage or early Advance.',unresolved=[],conflicts=[],alternatives=['An embedding service may terminate removed nodes; such policy is outside this live-node library check.'])),monitors=[dict(id='m_removed_read',checker_id='safe_returned_fence',event='read_result',binding_ids=['bind_singleton_read','bind_removal_read'],grounding=g,admission_alias='admission',applicability_conditions=[])],observable_properties=[dict(checker_id='safe_returned_fence',kind='event_implication',trigger=dict(field='event',op='eq',value='read_result'),antecedent=dict(field='read_returned',op='eq',value=True),assertion=dict(field='covers_completed_write',op='eq',value=True),identity_fields=['case','read_id'],description='If this uniquely identified post-write read receives a certificate, its fence must cover the actual completed write. Absence of a certificate is permitted pending behavior.')],uncertainties=['The check observes a library read certificate and a minimal integer state machine, not an external service endpoint.','Embedding applications that immediately stop removed nodes do not expose this path.','The stepdown control has no completed read; only bounded absence of unsafe output is established.'])\n# A same-event field is not an alias reference in the monitor language; use independent constant completion predicate instead.\nplan['harness']['prerequisites'][0]['conditions']=[dict(field='new_value',op='eq',value=1),dict(field='write_completed',op='eq',value=True)]\ns=s.replace('\\\"read_returned\\\":len(reads[1])>0,','\\\"read_returned\\\":len(reads[1])>0,\\\"write_completed\\\":writeIndex>0 && applied[2]>=writeIndex && values[2]==1,')\nPath('removed_read_check_test.go').write_text(s)\njson.dump(plan,open('plan9.json','w'),indent=2)\nsub=dict(action='check',candidate=cs,plan_path='plan9.json',harness_path='removed_read_check_test.go',rationale='Submit a fresh fixed safety check and attributed obligation for stale read certification after removal; preserve permitted pending control.',feedback=dict(ref_ids=[c['id'],'2b93f866725c4c13ac2c78db651dcb67','s_read_contract','s_removal_option','s_config_commit'],answered='Exploration reached final singleton membership with old node absent but still StateLeader when stepdown was false. The successor became term-3 leader and applied the write at index 6; only then the old node emitted ReadState index 4 while applied/value remained 4/0. With stepdown enabled no certificate was emitted. This supplies construction knowledge; fixed execution remains separate. The inspected API provides no mandatory immediate-stop duty and preserves ReadOnlySafe independently of the optional removal stepdown.',remaining=['Fresh execution and checker correspondence against the implication oracle.'],understanding='unchanged',rationale='The same actual history establishes the writer and reader relationship; no claim rests on isolated fragments or context reuse.'))\njson.dump(sub,open('submission9.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\npython3 make_check9.py\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-03_11-17-23-etcd_raft-real-run --submission submission9.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
